# Provider plugins and the local backend scaffold — re-created by `tofu init`.
.terraform/

# State. It lives in S3 (see bootstrap.sh); a local copy here means someone ran
# without the backend configured, and it contains generated passwords.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Saved plans — binary, environment-specific, and can embed sensitive values.
*.tfplan
*.plan.bin

# envs/*.tfvars ARE COMMITTED, deliberately. A project's .tfvars IS its
# infrastructure definition — region, sizes, node counts, which AMI. Keeping it
# out of git would mean the one file describing what this environment actually
# is exists only on somebody's laptop, which defeats the point of writing the
# infrastructure down at all.
#
# It holds no secrets: project name, region, size preset, an SSH key NAME, an
# alerting email. Anything genuinely secret does not belong here — generated
# passwords live in the state file (S3, never committed) and application
# secrets live in the config bucket.
#
# If you find yourself wanting to put a credential in a .tfvars, that is the
# signal it belongs somewhere else, not the signal to gitignore this.

# The lock file IS normally committed to pin provider versions. It is ignored
# here because this is a skeleton: a project generates its own on first init
# for the platform it actually runs on.
.terraform.lock.hcl
